* Demand (measured)

Found by the demand scan of vla-entity-property-table-on-demand
(.vla-demand.py, 1416 AutoLISP files): code that runs today calls COM
properties of the APPLICATION / DOCUMENT objects that cador does not have:

  ActiveDocument (9 calls, has)   SupportPath (7)   Application (3)
  Preferences (3)   Layers (2, has)   Layouts (2)   Blocks (2, has)
  Files (2)   ActiveProfile (1)   Profiles (1)   Documents (1, has)
  Active (1)

Callers: EPUREE (src/comu.lsp -- epuree:delete-layout-by-name-safe walks
vla-get-layouts / vla-item by name; a Documents walk tests vla-get-Active)
and its SNCF upstream (SNCF_startup.lsp reads and sets
Preferences -> Files -> SupportPath, reads Profiles / ActiveProfile).

* To do (per the vla-entity-property-table-on-demand discipline)

For each: classify against both vendors first (AGENTS.md, dialect
divergence), probe what the vendor returns, then implement with a test:
  - Document.Layouts collection + Item by name (needs layouts in the
    headless model -- shared with alref's CHSPACE);
  - Document.Active (T for the active document of the Documents
    collection);
  - Preferences -> Files -> SupportPath (the ACAD support path string --
    which host value backs it: (getenv "ACAD"), SRCHPATH?) and its setter;
  - Preferences -> Profiles -> ActiveProfile.

* Measured (probe-triage2, 2026-10-04)

BricsCAD V26 macOS (job 16923716753) and BricsCAD V25 Windows (job 16923716756 --
the Windows runner has V25, not V26: corrected 2026-10-05), the same:
  type of (vlax-get-acad-object)               VLA-OBJECT
  Layouts count                                3 (a French template)
  Layouts names (vlax-for)                     ("Présentation1" "Présentation2" "Model")
  Layouts Item "Model" name                    "Model"
  Layouts Item "NoSuchLayout"                  error (Automation Error E_FAIL /
                                               8020001a "Clé introuvable")
  Document Active                              :VLAX-TRUE
  Preferences Files SupportPath: type          STR
  ... = (getenv "ACAD")                        T
  Preferences Profiles ActiveProfile: type     STR
AutoCAD 2022 (accoreconsole, job 16923765011): (vlax-get-acad-object) is nil
headless -- no COM to measure; its documented object model is the same.

* Done (clautolisp 2.2.179)

- Document.Layouts: a live collection derived from the layout blocks
  (*Paper_Space -> "Layout1", then *Model_Space -> "Model", BricsCAD's walk
  order); Layout objects carry Name, ObjectName AcDbLayout, ModelType,
  TabOrder, Block. Item by name, missing name -> :com-item-not-found.
  A fresh cador drawing has ONE paper layout (one *Paper_Space record), so
  Count is 2 where a vendor template gives 3.
- Document.Active: :VLAX-TRUE for the Application's ActiveDocument,
  :VLAX-FALSE otherwise. :VLAX-TRUE / :VLAX-FALSE are now predefined
  self-valued symbols (they were unbound, i.e. nil) --
  vlax-boolean-properties-return-t covers the other boolean properties.
- Preferences.Files.SupportPath: the runtime support path joined with ";"
  (read/write; findfile / load follow it). (getenv "ACAD") and
  (setenv "ACAD" ...) are that same support path, as measured.
- Preferences.Profiles.ActiveProfile: CPROFILE (read).
Not done: Layout.Delete (EPUREE's epuree:delete-layout-by-name-safe catches
the error) -- cador has no paper layout besides *Paper_Space to delete.
